From 402d272db8ee2720d09e8d04f583e36ee9461dc7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: legsmechanical <joshgaine@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 29 Jun 2026 08:43:21 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] feat(manager): serve remote UI for the active overtake
 tool
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The remote UI was slot-only: discovery keyed on the per-slot synth_module
shm key and params on the synth:/fxN: prefixes. An overtake tool (e.g.
davebox) occupies no chain slot — its DSP is dlopen'd in the shim as
overtake_dsp_gen_inst and addressed via the "overtake_dsp:<key>" prefix
that shim_handle_param_special already serves on the shadow_param ring
(the exact path shadow_ui.js uses). So no shim/C change is needed; the
manager just has to use that prefix.

- handleSubscribe: probe overtake_dsp:module_id; if a tool answers, serve
  its web_ui.html as the slot's custom UI and seed from overtake_dsp:state,
  then skip the chain-slot path (the user is in the tool).
- setParam: route overtake_dsp:-prefixed writes through the reliable
  shadow_param ring (request_type=1), which the shim routes to the overtake
  DSP. The fast web_param_set ring has no overtake_dsp branch and would
  mis-route to a chain slot. Also lifts the fast ring's 255B value cap.
- refreshLoop: overtake-tool backstop so live sync survives with no synth.

Manager-only, additive; degrades cleanly to the existing slot path when no
overtake tool is active. Cross-compiles clean (ARM64). Pairs with davebox
get_param("module_id")/web_ui prefix change.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SccYnQe2WXaEwGhP1T7nuT
