MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

An overtake tool (e.g. davebox) is not a chain slot, so it doesn't belong
under a Slot tab — the shell gated custom UIs on a slot having a loaded
module (hasAnyModule), so davebox's served UI never showed. Add a Tool tab
alongside Master FX (also a non-slot view):

- Manager: subscribe_tool/unsubscribe_tool (discover via overtake_dsp:module_id,
  serve web_ui.html under component "tool", seed overtake_dsp:state) +
  refetch_tool (params-only re-read for the web UI's live-sync poll, so it
  doesn't re-send custom_ui and reload the iframe). refreshLoop backstop fans
  overtake_dsp:state to tool subscribers. Reverts the earlier slot-path overtake
  serving (slots stay slot-only).
- Shell (remote-ui.js): tool state + view; subscribe/switchSlot/renderSlot
  generalized for the "tool" pseudo-slot; tool_info / custom_ui("tool") /
  overtake_dsp: param_update routing; iframe get/set/seed handlers tool-aware
  (routes sets on slot 0 — manager dispatches by key prefix).
- remote-api.js: add resubscribe() (was missing in iframe mode → davebox's poll
  would have thrown); posts {type:"resubscribe"} → parent issues refetch_tool.
- template: Tool tab button.

Compiles ARM clean; JS syntax-checked; strings embedded in binary. NOT yet
deployed (device busy). Pairs with davebox get_param("module_id")/web_ui prefix.

