Subject: [PATCH 4/5] perf(remote-ui): rev-gate the overtake-tool poll to skip
 the heavy snapshot read

handleRefetchTool was doing a full overtake_dsp:state read (which serializes all
of davebox's notes/hits/steps) on every browser poll. Now it first reads the
cheap overtake_dsp:rui_poll digest (rev:on:tick:bpm) and only does the full
fetchAllParams when rev changes (a content edit). While playing with no edit it
pushes just the moving playhead; when nothing changed it does no shm-heavy work.
Falls back to a full fetch if the tool predates the rui_poll key. Also gates the
handler on toolSub as a safety belt (an unsubscribed client triggers no read).
Per-client rev/tick cache on ruClient, reset on (un)subscribe.
